# Cloud-agent Linear handoff

Canonical detail: **`docs/cloud-agent-linear-handoff.md`**.

When this session is a **Cloud Agent**, **background agent**, or other remote agent, after it
**authors or implements a plan** (planning PR or runtime PR): emit a copy-paste **local-agent
Linear handoff**. A local Cursor agent with Linear MCP `ready` applies it. GitHub PR linkbacks do
not replace Linear.

## Emit when

- Linear MCP is `needsAuth`, empty-tools, or failed; **or**
- the session is remote even if Linear later succeeds (write **Posted in-session** plus the same
  verbatim comments for verification).

## Same-session destinations (all three)

1. Slice doc `## Local-agent Linear handoff`
2. PR body Follow-ups (verbatim comments; include PR URL)
3. Closeout field **Local-agent Linear handoff** in `docs/agent-session-closeout.md`

Required payload: issue IDs; exact status or **do not change**; verbatim comment markdown; parent
row or **none**; **Do not** list; already-posted flag.

## Local agent

Apply verbatim. Skip duplicates that already contain the same PR URL and facts. Honor **do not
change** over the generic In Progress / Done table.

## Do not

Invent Linear tokens. Skip Linear because GitHub has a bot linkback. Collapse comments to
one-liners. Mark In Progress / Done when the handoff or user forbade it.
